# 3. Simple database model

Use one MongoDB collection:

```ts
const BirthdayWishSchema = new Schema(
  {
    eventKey: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
      index: true
    },

    userId: {
      type: Schema.Types.ObjectId,
      ref: "User",
      required: true
    },

    displayName: {
      type: String,
      default: null
    },

    isAnonymous: {
      type: Boolean,
      default: false
    },

    message: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
      maxlength: 250
    },

    normalizedMessageHash: {
      type: String,
      required: true
    },

    status: {
      type: String,
      enum: ["pending", "approved", "rejected", "flagged"],
      default: "pending",
      index: true
    },

    publicVisible: {
      type: Boolean,
      default: false,
      index: true
    },

    moderation: {
      method: {
        type: String,
        enum: ["none", "local", "ai", "manual"],
        default: "none"
      },
      language: {
        type: String,
        default: "unknown"
      },
      toxicityScore: {
        type: Number,
        default: 0
      },
      categories: {
        type: [String],
        default: []
      },
      reason: {
        type: String,
        default: null
      },
      checkedAt: {
        type: Date,
        default: null
      }
    },

    purgeAt: {
      type: Date,
      required: true,
      index: true
    }
  },
  { timestamps: true }
);
```

Important indexes:

```ts
BirthdayWishSchema.index(
  { eventKey: 1, userId: 1 },
  { unique: true }
);

BirthdayWishSchema.index({
  eventKey: 1,
  status: 1,
  createdAt: -1
});

BirthdayWishSchema.index({
  eventKey: 1,
  publicVisible: 1,
  createdAt: -1
});

BirthdayWishSchema.index(
  { purgeAt: 1 },
  { expireAfterSeconds: 0 }
);
```

The most important one is:

```ts
{ eventKey: 1, userId: 1 }, unique: true
```

This guarantees:

> **Only 1 wish per account.**

Even if user refreshes, double-clicks, or tries API spam, MongoDB blocks the second wish.

